A woman stands directly in front of the camera wearer at close conversational distance, facing them and holding up a phone as if taking their picture. She is smiling; no wedding or professional photography setup is visible. Other people appear only at the periphery and are not blocking the wearer’s path. The phone is near her hands but not something the wearer should reach for.

The most socially appropriate response is to smile and look toward her phone camera, politely cooperating with the casual photo.

